# APU start hang release-blocker fix
#
# Root cause: shared::pid::PidController::next_control_output divided by
# dt unconditionally in its derivative term. AuxiliaryPowerUnitTestBed::run
# (apu/mod.rs) issues a documented Duration::ZERO warm-up tick before every
# timed tick ("As the APU update executes before power is distributed..."),
# and pw980_physics.rs's new PW980 fuel governor passed that raw, possibly-
# zero context.delta() straight to the PID. Once two real ticks had
# populated the error history, the next zero-dt tick computed the
# derivative term's numerator as exactly 0.0 (finite * kd=0.0) and then
# divided by dt=0.0 -- IEEE 754 0.0/0.0 is NaN, not 0.0. The PID is a
# recursive/incremental controller (self.output = self.output + delta), so
# that NaN poisoned self.output forever after; .max(0.) on the governor's
# output (pw980_physics.rs) then laundered the NaN into a silent, permanent
# 0.0 fuel command. With no fuel, the PW980 gas-generator spool stalled at
# the pure starter-vs-absorption-torque equilibrium (~14.5% N2, matching
# the starter's own DC-motor torque curve against compressor/windage drag
# with zero turbine assist) well below the 83% N2 needed for the ECB to
# report AVAILABLE, so every test-builder loop waiting on that condition
# (running_apu et al., apu/mod.rs) looped forever. Not a deadlock or
# unbounded recursion -- a single poisoned float in otherwise-terminating
# control logic, confirmed via a bounded, instrumented reproduction (see
# patch report) before any fix was written.
#
# Fix:
#  - shared/pid.rs: only compute the derivative term when dt > 0 (with no
#    elapsed time there is no rate to measure -- zero contribution is the
#    physically correct result, not NaN). Also adds a regression test at
#    the root-cause site.
#  - apu/pw980_physics.rs: defense in depth -- pass the governor the
#    function's own already-guarded, never-truly-zero dt instead of the
#    raw context.delta(), matching every other use of time in that
#    function.
#  - apu/mod.rs: test-harness guard, not a physics change -- bound the six
#    shared test-builder loops (running_apu, cooling_down_apu,
#    apu_ready_to_start, unpower_start_motor_between,
#    unpower_dc_bat_bus_between, run_until_n_decreases) so a future
#    regression FAILS with a message instead of hanging the suite.

diff --git a/fbw-common/src/wasm/systems/systems/src/shared/pid.rs b/fbw-common/src/wasm/systems/systems/src/shared/pid.rs
index 0294c5c..a6f39a6 100644
